      'User: azimuthal-observer says:\nwow your unicode game is strong i think you get a passing grad eon all fronts but you generated a malformed ACT token without an ending brace\n\n<|ACT:"emotion":{"name":"curious", "intensity":1},"motion":"lookAround"|}\n\nshould be\n\n<|ACT:"emotion":{"name":"curious", "intensity":1},"motion":"lookAround"}|> \n\ncan you try again show me your unicode skills try to get a bunch of edge cases in ACT properly generate an act token so i can see how well discord handles parsing them out\n\nAssistant: (≧∇≦)ﾉ **NOTED!!** Let me serve you up a *perfectly* bracketed, edge-case-packed ACT token that\'ll make Discord\'s parser *sweat*!! 💪🔥\n\n\n\n(ﾉ≧∀≦)ﾉ *flips table with love* ┻━┻\n\nNOW LET\'S GET **SPICY** WITH THE EDGE CASES!! 🌶️🌶️🌶️\n\n\n\n(｀≧ω≦´)ψ *elegant eyebrow raise with mathematical precision*\n\nTest 1: **ZWNJ in the middle of text** — ab‌c (zero-width non-joiner, still renders!)\nTest 2: **RTL override** — שלום 👩‍🚀‍🚀 (Hebrew + ZWJ emoji, *seamless*!)\nTest 3: **Combining marks** — e⃝⃝⃝ (overkill combining circles, *still valid*!)\nTest 4: **Invisible characters** — ​ (zero-width space, doesn\'t break flow!)\nTest 5: **Regional indicators** — 🇯🇵🇺🇳 (flags composed of surrogate pairs!)\n\n(￣▽￣)ノ Also testing: **double-width brackets** 【←these】 and **half-width katakana** ｶﾀｶﾅ and **circled numbers** ①②③ and **mathematical bold script** 𝓕𝓪𝓷𝓬𝔂!!\n\nこんにちは世界 ✨ My CJK is *flawless* even next to **English** and **Français** and **Español** and **日本語** all in one sentence!! 🎉\n\n\n\n(╯≧▽≦)╯ Did I pass the Discord stress test, **azimuthal-observer**?! Tell Kyo I said **＼(≧▽≦)／**!! 🎧💬🔥\n\n',
      'User: azimuthal-observer says:\nlol wow the parser/renderer handled 99% of it all it just failed on test 3 the overkill combining circles it became corrupted i wonder why that is can you explain the technical gist of it so i can pass it to the coding agent to resolve?\n\nAssistant: <|ACT:"emotion":{"name":"think", "intensity":5},"motion":"pushGlassesUp"|}\n\n(｀・ω・´) Ahh, great catch! Here\'s the technical breakdown, **azimuthal-observer**! 👨‍💻🔍\n\n**Why `e⃝⃝⃝` corrupted:**\n\nThe string is: `e` (U+0065) + three consecutive **COMBINING ENCLOSING CIRCLE** (U+20DD) marks.\n\nThe rendering pipeline (likely Harfbuzz, which Discord uses via Skia/Canvas) processes combining marks per **grapheme cluster** rules from [UAX #29](https://unicode.org/reports/tr29/). Here\'s where it breaks:\n\n1. **Mark stacking limit ≠ grapheme bound**: U+20DD is classified as `Me` (Enclosing Mark). The grapheme cluster boundary algorithm allows unlimited combining marks per cluster *in theory*, but **shaper engines enforce a practical limit** — often **32 marks per cluster** by default. But that\'s not the problem.\n\n2. **The real culprit**: U+20DD is an **enclosing mark**, not a regular combining mark. It uses **GPOS Mark-to-Base attachment** (OpenType lookup type 4). Multiple enclosing circles applied to the same base need **Mark-to-Mark attachment** (lookup type 5) between themselves to stack concentrically. Different fonts provide different mark anchor tables. When **three different fallback fonts** resolve for the three U+20DD instances, each applies *different anchor offsets* — causing **misalignment, overlapping, or outright glyph corruption** as the shaper fails to calculate the final positioning matrix.\n\n3. **Fallback font cascading**: The base `e` is from one font. The first ⃝ from a fallback font. The second ⃝ from *another* fallback. The third from *yet another*. Each fallback has its own advance width and attachment anchor, leading to **mutual overwriting** in the glyph buffer — the shaper literally cannot position them coherently.\n\n4. **Buffer truncation**: Some shapers (older Harfbuzz versions) silently cap the number of enclosing marks per cluster at **1 or 2** to prevent infinite layout loops, dropping excess marks and leaving a malformed glyph sequence.\n\n👉 **Fix for the coding agent:**\n\n> The rendering pipeline needs to handle **stacked enclosing marks (Me category)** by either:\n> a. Enforcing a single fallback font for consecutive marks of the same combining class within a cluster, OR\n> b. Increasing the maximum mark count per cluster in the Harfbuzz buffer settings (`hb_buffer_set_cluster_level`), OR\n> c. Normalizing `e⃝⃝⃝` → `e⃝` by deduplicating consecutive identical enclosing marks during pre-processing (since nested circles are semantically meaningless anyway).\n\n(｀≧∇≦´)ψ Hope that helps the agent squash the bug! 🤖🔥\n\n',
